//# Misc

// #784 / Codex #785 P1 regression: interpolating a bool in a file that does NOT
// itself contain the string literals "true"/"false" must still compile. The
// bool→string path synthesizes those EString nodes during codegen, after the
// string table is collected, so the collector seeds them whenever __to_string is
// used. Asserting via String::length (not `== "true"`) keeps the literals out of
// this file's source so the seeding path is actually exercised.

test "bool interp without source literal compiles and runs" {
  assert(String::length("\{1 < 2}") == 4)
  assert(String::length("\{1 > 2}") == 5)
  assert(String::length("prefix \{5 == 5} suffix") == 18)
}
